അഞ്ച് positive parts-ുള്ള cutlet partition family-യിൽ internal calculation-day gate boundary ആവശ്യമായപ്പോൾ exact filtered count brute-force ആയി പരിശോധിക്കുന്ന clean Stage 1 regression. fixture total gate gaps 7, parts 5, required prefix boundary 3 ആണ്.

Hamlet, valid count സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, ആദ്യ ഭാഗം സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, രണ്ടാം ഭാഗം സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, മൂന്നാം ഭാഗം സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, നാലാം ഭാഗം സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, അഞ്ചാം ഭാഗം സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, prefix sum സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Cordelia, boundary-hit flag സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, output സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: counters.

Scene I: count=0, first=1.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero: You are nothing.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero: You are a hero.

Act II: first loop.

Scene I: first 3 കടന്നാൽ result; total 7, five positive parts ആയതിനാൽ first max 3.
[Enter Juliet and Prospero]
Juliet: Am I better than the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to act VII.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero: You are a hero.

Act III: second loop.

Scene I: second 3 കടന്നാൽ first കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Enter Romeo and Prospero]
Romeo: Am I better than the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to act VI.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are a hero.

Act IV: third loop.

Scene I: third 3 കടന്നാൽ second കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Enter Othello and Prospero]
Othello: Am I better than the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VIII.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Macbeth]
Prospero: You are a hero.

Scene II: fourth 3 കടന്നാൽ third കൂട്ടുന്നു.
[Enter Macbeth and Prospero]
Macbeth: Am I better than the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VII.

Scene III: fifth = 7-first-second-third-fourth.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between the sum of a big big hero and the sum of a big hero and a hero and Juliet.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and Romeo.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and Othello.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and Macbeth.

Scene IV: fifth positive ആണോ എന്ന് പരിശോധിക്കുന്നു.
[Enter Lady Macbeth and Prospero]
Lady Macbeth: Am I worse than a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene IX.

Scene V: prefix boundary 3 hit പരിശോധിക്കുന്നു.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero: You are nothing.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as Juliet.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Ophelia and Prospero]
Ophelia: Am I as good as the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VI.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of Juliet and Romeo.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Ophelia and Prospero]
Ophelia: Am I as good as the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VI.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of Juliet and Romeo. You are as good as the sum of yourself and Othello.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Ophelia and Prospero]
Ophelia: Am I as good as the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VI.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of Juliet and Romeo. You are as good as the sum of yourself and Othello. You are as good as the sum of yourself and Macbeth.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Ophelia and Prospero]
Ophelia: Am I as good as the sum of a big hero and a hero?
Prospero: If not, let us proceed to scene IX.

Scene VI: valid count കൂട്ടുന്നു.
